//! task: write
//! ask: Write a function that is true when x lies between lo and hi inclusive, using Exsecutor's comparison and connective words.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §8.4, §8.6
//! explain: The six comparisons are the words `lt le gt ge eq ne`, and the connectives are `et` (and) and `vel` (or). `et` and `vel` short-circuit. Comparison is non-associative: `a lt b lt c` is EXS-E0201. `u1` is the one-bit type used for truth values.

publica functio intra(x: u32, lo: u32, hi: u32) -> u1 {
    si x ge lo et x le hi {
        redde 1;
    }
    redde 0;
}
